---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Cookie Policy - ArceApps">
  <div class="bg-surface-subtle py-16 dark:bg-dark-surface-subtle md:py-20">
    <!-- Language Toggle -->
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 mb-8 flex justify-center">
      <div class="inline-flex gap-2 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface-raised p-1.5 shadow-sm dark:border-dark-border dark:bg-dark-surface-raised">
        <a href="/es/cookies" class="px-4 py-2 rounded-lg text-on-surface-variant dark:text-dark-on-surface-variant hover:bg-gray-200 dark:hover:bg-gray-700 transition-colors focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary focus-visible:outline-none">
          🇪🇸 Español
        </a>
        <span class="px-4 py-2 rounded-lg bg-primary text-white font-medium shadow-sm cursor-default">
          🇺🇸 English
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <article class="container mx-auto px-4 max-w-4xl">
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4 text-on-surface dark:text-dark-on-surface">Cookie Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant dark:text-dark-on-surface-variant">Last updated: August 12, 2026</p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-slate dark:prose-invert mx-auto rounded-[2rem] border border-border bg-surface-raised p-6 shadow-xl shadow-primary/5 dark:border-dark-border dark:bg-dark-surface-raised md:p-10 prose-a:focus-visible:ring-2 prose-a:focus-visible:ring-primary prose-a:focus-visible:outline-none prose-a:rounded-sm">
        <h2>What are cookies?</h2>
        <p>
          Cookies are small text files that websites store in your browser. They are used for many purposes: remembering
          preferences, keeping you logged in, or measuring how a website is used.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies used on this website</h2>
        <p>
          This website is free, ad-free, and does not use advertising, personalization or profiling cookies. The only
          cookies it can use are Google Analytics statistics cookies, and only <strong>after you explicitly accept</strong> them
          in the consent banner.
        </p>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Cookie</th>
              <th>Purpose</th>
              <th>Duration</th>
              <th>Provider</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><code>_ga</code></td>
              <td>Distinguishes users (anonymous identifier)</td>
              <td>2 years</td>
              <td>Google LLC (Google Analytics)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>_ga_&lt;container-id&gt;</code></td>
              <td>Stores session and campaign state</td>
              <td>2 years</td>
              <td>Google LLC (Google Analytics)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>_gid</code></td>
              <td>Distinguishes users (anonymous identifier)</td>
              <td>24 hours</td>
              <td>Google LLC (Google Analytics)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>_gat_*</code></td>
              <td>Rate limiting of requests</td>
              <td>1 minute</td>
              <td>Google LLC (Google Analytics)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>
          If you reject statistics cookies, <strong>none of the cookies above are installed</strong>. Google Analytics then only
          receives aggregated, anonymous information that cannot identify your device, used to estimate traffic patterns
          (Google Consent Mode).
        </p>

        <h2>Your consent</h2>
        <p>
          When you visit this website for the first time, a banner asks you to accept or reject statistics cookies. Nothing
          is collected until you make a choice, and rejecting is as easy as accepting. Your choice is stored in your own
          browser (<code>localStorage</code>, key <code>cookie-consent</code>), and the banner will not be shown again on that
          device.
        </p>
        <p>
          Even if you accept, we never enable advertising, user-data or personalization signals: no data is collected for
          advertising, nothing is sold to third parties, and no sensitive data is collected.
        </p>

        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          The statistics cookies belong to Google Analytics, a service of Google LLC. Google uses the collected data to
          analyze how the website is used and to prepare reports. Google's privacy policy is available at
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>How to change or withdraw your consent</h2>
        <p>
          You can withdraw or change your choice at any time by clearing the <code>cookie-consent</code> entry in your
          browser's <code>localStorage</code> (or all site data) for this website. The banner will then appear again on your
          next visit.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you have any questions about this cookie policy, please use the
          <a href="/about-me#contact">contact form</a>.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 p-6 bg-primary/5 rounded-xl border border-primary/20">
          <p>
            © Arce Apps<br />
            Madrid - Spain
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
